{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979839-ghost-gate-destroys-equipment","id":979839,"title":"Ghost Gate Destroys Equipment?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-01T14:01:38-07:00","id":979839,"title":"Ghost Gate Destroys Equipment?","content":"I'm trying to parse this spell here.<br /> <br /> If I'm reading it as is, passing through a Ghost Gate converts you and everything you pull with you into ephemera.<br /> <br /> Then, when the spell ends, you turn back to physical matter, but your clothing remains there as ephemera? And when retrieved with Touch of the Grave, they have a durability of 1, a limited duration in this world, and break into ephemera when destroyed?<br /> <br /> If that's accurate, how does a mage keep their things from being destroyed whenever they want to go on a Twilight jaunt, or is that just to discourage that being a common thing?<br /> I'd assume artifacts are unaffected, but what about Perfected metals, which are supposed to turn from ephemera and back again constantly anyway? What about imbued items? Is Ghost Gate the ever-hungry maw of destruction?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T15:00:51-07:00","id":979871,"title":"","content":"If you want to enter Twilight without destroying your stuff, use Spirit instead. Twilit Body does not have these same downsides, but it also won't help you interact with Ghosts.<br /> <br /> I would assume that the process of turning into <i>Death</i>-attuned Ephemera is just naturally destructive, given that Spirit-attuned Ephemera has no such issue. Similar to how Mind's only way to enter Twilight doesn't let you turn your body or clothes into ephemera; only your mind enters Twilight. Each one interacts with Twilight differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:34:39-07:00","id":979926,"title":"","content":"I noticed the same thing and posted about it. Between ignoring both structure and durability, and requiring only arcanum 3, it's far and away the best spell for destroying objects in the game. You'd need matter 5 unmaking to replicate that, and that gets fast less Reach. No errata though, so I assume it's intended. <br /> <br /> If you want to get objects into Death attuned twilight without destroying them you need that one Matter spell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T16:44:38-07:00","id":979932,"title":"","content":"Now we know why the frugal ghost has always favored the plain white sheet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12136-jacobkosh","name":"jacobkosh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T18:01:58-07:00","id":979970,"title":"","content":"The Reach option seems to imply that you can make items transition to Twilight without being destroyed. I'd certainly allow a Reach option to do that even if that particular one doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-01T19:26:27-07:00","id":980007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979839-ghost-gate-destroys-equipment?p=979926#post979926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I noticed the same thing and posted about it. Between ignoring both structure and durability, and requiring only arcanum 3, it's far and away the best spell for destroying objects in the game. You'd need matter 5 unmaking to replicate that, and that gets fast less Reach. No errata though, so I assume it's intended.<br /> <br /> If you want to get objects into Death attuned twilight without destroying them you need that one Matter spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is strange, now that I notice it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>We don't allow mages to cast spells, since this is the most unbalancing rule of all.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5226-jachra","name":"Jachra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"265"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}